Yesterday Martelly swore a nine-member new preliminary electoral council (Provisional Electoral Council or CEP).
Martelly has achieved a CEP five times in the past four years.
Last month, the presidential commission recommended the resignation of the earlier National Electoral Council. This is part of a package of measures so that new elections will be held in the country.
The commission was set up by Martelly in response to the widespread protests against the government that have taken place since October.
The sometimes violent protests arose due to the lack of elections, some of which should have taken place since 2011.
About 60 cases have been reported of defective iPods overheating. In total, this led to six fires and four people with minor burns.
