Of the 1400 people surveyed before the 2010 federal election, the number of people who opposed the fact that Australia became a republic increased by 8 percent since 2008.
Demissionary Prime Minister Julia Gillard said during the campaign for the 2010 federal election that Australia should become a republic after the reign of Queen Elizabeth II.
34 percent of the participants of this poll stood behind this point of view. They want Queen Elizabeth II to be Australia's last monarch.
29 percent of respondents felt that Australia should become a republic as soon as it is possible, and at the other end, 31 percent said that should never happen.
