There are felines of medium size between eating prey of medium size, from hares to antelopes and deer.
In addition, there are many small cats (such as loose cats that are kept as pets) that hunt for larger numbers of small prey, such as insects, rodents, lizards and birds.
Their success stems from the idea of a niche, a special job that every cat doesn’t compete with others.
Lions are the most social cats and live in large groups called troops.
Troops consist of one to three adult males who are related to each other and also have up to thirty females and cubs.
The women are normally closely related to each other and form a large family of sisters and daughters.
A bunch of lions behaves pretty much the same as a pack of wolves or dogs, animals that are surprisingly similar to lions (but not like other big felines), and that are very deadly to their prey.
The tiger is a versatile athlete and can climb (although not good), swimming, jumping great distances and has five times as much traction as a strong person.
The tiger belongs to the same group (Genus Panthera) as lions, leopards and jaguars. These four felines are the only ones who can roar.
A tiger doesn’t roar with full power like a lion. It’s more as if he growls a whole sentence.
Ocelotten’s favorite meal is small animals. They catch monkeys, snakes, rodents and birds if they succeed. The ocelot hunts almost exclusively for animals that are much smaller than it is itself.
Scholars suspect that ocelots use their sense of smell to hunt small animals (their prey), by smelling on the ground where they have been.
They can see very well in the dark due to night vision and move very unobtrusively. Ocelots hunt prey by making themselves one with the environment and then jumping into their prey.
When a small group of organisms (a small population) detaches from the large population from which they originate (for example, by moving over a mountain range or river, or if they are moved to another island, from where they cannot return easily), they are often located in a different environment than before.
In this new environment there are other raw materials and other enemies, so the new population has to behave differently or adapt in order to cope with the competition.
Because they still need the same adjustments as before, the original population has not changed at all.
As the new population began to adapt to the new environment, they also began to look less and less like the other population.
After thousands or even millions of years, the two populations will be so different in appearance that you can no longer call them the same species.
This process is called species formation and simply involves the formation of new species. Species formation is an unavoidable consequence and a very important part of evolution.
