The Great Pyramid of Gizah is the only one of the seven wonders of the world.
The Great Pyramid was built by the Egyptians in the third century BC and belongs to the numerous large pyramid structures in honor of a deceased pharaoh.
The Plateau of Giza or 'pyramides of Gizah' in the Egyptian valley of the dead contains several pyramids (of which the Great Pyramid is the largest), several small tombs, a number of temples and the great sphinx.
The great pyramid was built to honor Pharaoh Khufu. Many of the smaller pyramids, tombs, and temples were built in tribute to the women and relatives of Khufu.
The up-bow sign looks like a V and the down-bow sign looks like a staple or a square whose bottom is missing.
Upper means that you have to start at the tip and push the bow away. Below means that you have to start at the arch frog (the spot where your hand holds the bow) and put on the bow.
An upward movement usually gives a softer sound, while a downward movement produces a stronger and more assertive sound.
