MS is a disease that affects the central nervous system. This includes the brain, the spine, and the optic nerve.
Research has shown that women are twice as likely to receive MS as men.
A couple may decide that it's not in their interest, or that of their child, to raise a baby.
These couples may choose to give up their baby for adoption.
With an adoption, the parents give up their parental rights, so that another couple can raise the child.
Discovering how the world works on the basis of the scientific method is the main goal of science. This method is the guideline for most scientific research.
Nevertheless, it is about more than just experiments; a experiment is a test to exclude one or more potential assumptions, place question marks and make observations, as a guideline for science research.
