Aristotle's views regarding science, including psychology, were accepted.
The West understood Greek philosophy and science less and less because the knowledge of Greek was diminishing.
With physiological and behavioral observations of rhythms, there is often a strong dependence on endogenous processes and production via the biological clock.
Most creatures, including bacteria, fungi, plants, and animals, live according to periodic rhythms. These aren’t just reactions to external periodic signals.
Biological clocks are self-sufficient oscillators that go through a cycle for a certain period of time, even if no external signals are issued for this.
Hershey's and Chase's experiment was one of the main indications that DNA was a genetic material.
Hershey and Chase used bacteriophages or viruses to implant their own DNA into a bacterium.
Two experiments were carried out. In one experiment the DNA in the phage was marked with a radioactive phosphorus and in the other experiment the protein of the phaage was marked with radioactive sulfur.
Mutations can have many different effects, depending on the type, the importance of the genetic material involved and whether the affected cells are germinate cells.
Only mutations in germinate cells are hereditary. Due to other mutations, cells can die or cancer can develop.
Nature tourism attracts people who like to visit nature reserves because they want to enjoy the landscape, including the flora and fauna.
On the spot you can hunt, fish, photograph, observe birds, go to parks and study the ecosystem.
An example is a visit to, photographing and learning about the orangutans in Borneo.
Every morning people go from small villages by car to their workplace and pass people whose workplace is located in the village where they just came from.
Everyone in this dynamic transport shuttle is somehow in contact with and supports a transport system based on private cars.
Science shows that because of this enormous carbon economy, the biosphere is no longer in the stable state, which allowed human evolution to take place over the past two million years.
Everyone participates in society and uses transport systems, and almost everyone complains about it.
In developed countries, problems with water quality or collapsing bridges are rare in comparison.
How is it that so many complaints arise with transport systems, why does it go wrong on a daily basis? Are transport technicians simply incapacitated? Or is it something more fundamental?
A traffic flow looks at the movements of individual drivers and vehicles between two points and the interactions that take place between the individuals.
Unfortunately, it is difficult to investigate the traffic flow, because the behavior of drivers cannot be predicted with 100% certainty.
Fortunately, drivers behave fairly predictably. This means that traffic flows show some degree of consistency and that there is something to be said about this mathematically.
Connections have been made between the three core properties to better reflect the traffic settlement: (1) intensity, (2) density and (3) speed.
With the help of those relationships, the planning, design and operation of road construction facilities is facilitated.
Insects began to be the first to fly animals. Thanks to their flying ability, they could more easily escape enemies and find more efficient food and mating partners.
The advantage of most insects is that they can fold their wings along the body.
As a result, they can hide from predators in a larger number of small places.
At the moment, only dragonflies and may flies cannot collapse their wings.
A few thousand years ago, Aristarchus said the solar system revolved around the sun.
There were people who thought he was right, but many people believed just the opposite; that the solar system moved around the Earth, and so did the Sun (and other stars).
This sounds pretty logical, because you don't feel the earth moving, do you?
The Amazon River is the world's largest and second-longest river and transports more than 8 times as much water as the second largest.
The Amazon is also the widest river on Earth and has a width of six miles in some places.
At least 20% of all the water flowing into the sea via the rivers comes from the Amazon.
The main flow of the Amazon River is 6,387 kilometers (3,980 miles) long. The water originates from thousands of smaller rivers.
Although the construction of stone pyramids continued until the end of the Old Kingdom, the pyramids of Giza remain unsurpassed in terms of size and technical excellence of construction.
The ancient Egyptians of the new kingdom admired the monument of their predecessors, which was more than a thousand years old at the time.
There are about 800 inhabitants living in Vatican City. This is the smallest independent country in the world and also the country with the lowest population.
Italian is the official language for the official communications and laws of Vatican City.
Italian is the language most commonly spoken by the people who work there, while Latin is widely used during religious ceremonies.
Everyone who lives in Vatican City is Roman Catholic.
People know the most basic chemical elements, such as gold, silver and copper from antiquity, because they can all be found in nature and it is fairly easy to mine them with primitive tools.
The philosopher Aristotle speculated that everything consists of a mixture of one or more of four elements: earth, water, air and fire.
This looked more like what we know from the four states of matter (in the same order): solid, liquid, gas and plasma, but he has also theorized that they transition into new substances in order to form into what we see.
Alloys are simply a combination of at least metals. As you probably know, the periodical system contains many elements.
Elements such as calcium and potassium fall under the metals. Of course, there are also metals such as silver and gold.
Alloys may also contain a small amount of non-metallic elements, for example carbon.
Everything in the universe is made up of matter. All matter consists of small particles called atoms.
Atoms are so incredibly small that a trillion atoms fit into the tip at the end of this sentence.
