As newer writing methods have emerged, the pen is unfortunately lowered in status and is used much less.
These days one writes messages on a computer screen without ever needing a pencil sharpener.
You may wonder what will happen to the keyboard as soon as something new comes on the market.
The atomic bomb works according to the principle that it takes energy to compose a nucleus with many protons and neutrons.
It's like you're pushing a heavy cart into a hill, and when the core is split up again, some of the energy is released.
Some atoms have an unstable nucleus, which means they fall apart at the slightest.
The surface of the moon is characterized by dust and rock. The crust is the outer layer of the moon.
The crust is approximately 70 km thick on the nearest side and 100 km thick on the other side.
The crust is thinner under the maria and thicker under the plateaus.
There may be more maren on the side, because the crust is thinner there. Lava could more easily get to the surface there.
Content theories aim to find out what moves people and what appeals to them.
This theory suggests that people have certain needs and/or desires that are internalized as they mature.
With these theories, they want to explore the reasons why certain people want to have certain things and what environmental factors they influence whether or not to do certain things.
Two popular content theories are Maslow's need pyramid and Hertzberg's Motivation-Hygiene theory.
In general, two practices come up when managers take charge of their former peers. In one course of action, they try to act as an equal.
This type of manager finds it difficult to make unpopular decisions and disciplinary actions, conducting evaluation interviews, delegating and appealing to people to their responsibilities.
On the other side of the spectrum, it transforms into an unrecognizable individual. He or she gets the feeling of having to change everything that the team has done so far, and wants to own everything.
Ultimately, the leader is responsible for the team's success and failure.
Often this behavior leads to a gap between the leaders and the team members.
Virtual teams have to live up to the same standards in terms of excellence as normal teams, although there are minor differences.
In most cases, virtual team members are the first point of contact for their direct physical group.
Often they are more independent than traditional team members. That’s because their teams can meet according to different time zones, which may not be understood by their local management.
The idea of a truly 'invisible team' (Larson and LaFasto, 1989, pp 109) is a unique element of a virtual team.
The 'invisible team' is the management team to whom each member reports. The invisible team also sets the standard for each member.
Why would an organization want to embark on the time-consuming process of setting up a learning organization? One of the goals for putting organizational learning concepts into practice is innovation.
Creativity and ingenuity come to light if all available resources are used effectively within the functional departments of an organization.
The result of this is that the process of an organization working together to overcome an obstacle can lead to a new innovative process to meet the needs of the customer.
In order to enable innovation in an organization, management must stimulate a culture in which innovation, shared knowledge and organizational learning are central.
According to Angel (2006), organizations can perform better with an approach based on the continuum model.
Neurobiological data provides physical evidence for a theoretical approach to cognition-examination. This allows the research area to be reduced and more accurate data can be collected.
The correlation between the pathology of the brain and behavior helps scientists during their research.
It has long been known that different types of brain injuries, traumas, wounds and tumors can affect behavior and lead to changes in mental ability.
Because there are more and more new technologies, we learn more and more about the structures and processes in the brain.
This provides us with a lot of information and material to develop simulation models with which we gain more insight into the processes of our mind.
AI immediately reminds most people about science fiction, but it is also an essential part of computer science. It is used in research on machine behavior, learning and intelligent adaptation.
Developing machines to automate tasks that require intelligent behavior is under research into AI.
Some examples are management, planning, the ability to answer customer diagnoses and questions and recognition of handwriting, voice and face.
These have become separate disciplines for finding solutions to real-life problems.
Today, this artificial intelligence system is widely used economically, medically, technically and militarily, as in various software applications for PCs and video games.
Many excursions are planned for each class. Often a teacher would take her students to places where a bus trip is not an option.
Thanks to technological developments, virtual excursions are now possible. This allows students from the classroom to view the artifacts in a museum, look inside an aquarium or see beautiful artworks.
Virtually sharing an excursion is also a fantastic way to look back on a journey and share experiences with future classes.
For example, Bennet School students in North Carolina design a website every year about their trip to the state's capital, which is reshaped each year and whose earlier versions are kept online to serve as a scrapbook.
Blogs can also help students write better. Often their grammar and spelling are still bad in the beginning, but this changes quickly because they have an audience.
Because students are often the most critical audience, the blogger strives to improve the writing and thus avoid criticism.
By blogging ‘students are also forced to learn more about the world around them’. The need to keep the public interested inspires students to be smart and interesting (Toto, 2004).
Blogging is a tool that inspires collaboration and encourages pupils to extend learning far beyond the traditional school day.
With good use, blogs 'help pupils develop analytically and think critically; by actively entering into the discussion on the internet, pupils can find their own place in the context of other people's material and at the same time determine their own position in certain issues' (Oravec, 2002).
The bilingual capital of Canada is charming Ottawa, full of art galleries and museums in which Canada is exhibited in the past and the future.
Further south you will find the Niagara Falls. In the north you will find the beautiful untouched Muskoka and even more.
This kind of thing makes Ontario, in the eyes of outsiders typically Canadian.
Further north, large areas are quite sparsely populated and some of these areas is even virtually uninhabited wilderness.
A population comparison that will amaze many: there are more African-Americans living in the United States than Canada's total population.
The East African islands are located along the east coast of Africa in the Indian Ocean.
Madagaskar is by far the largest and in terms of fauna it is almost a separate continent.
Most of the smaller islands are made up of independent countries or are connected to France and they are known as luxurious beach resorts.
The Arabs also took the Islamic faith with them, after which it spread widely on the Comoros and Mayotte.
The Portuguese explorer Vasco da Gama discovered the cape route from Europe to India, which marked the beginning of European influence and colonization in the 15th century.
The region borders southern and west on the Atlantic Ocean and north on the Sahel region.
Women: Female travelers are advised to say that they are married, whether or not that is true.
Also, it helps to put on rings (not too pricey-looking rings).
Women should keep in mind that cultural differences can lead to behavior that they see as intimidating and that it is customary to be followed, to be caught by the arm, etc.
Be clear when you reject a man and don’t be afraid to stand your guy (cultural differences don’t talk this right!).
The modern city of Casablanca was founded in the 10th century BC by Berber fishermen. The city was used as a strategic port by the Phoenicians, Romans and Merinids and was known as Anfa.
The Portuguese devastated the port and rebuilt it under the name Casa Branca. After an earthquake in 1755 they left the city again.
The sultan of Morocco rebuilt the city and called it Daru l-Bayad. The Spanish traders who established their trading base here gave it the name Casablanca.
In Morocco, Casablanca is one of the least interesting places for shopping.
Arounding the old Medina you will find many places where you can buy traditional Moroccan stuff, such as tagines, pots, leather products, hookahs and other gadgets, but it is purely aimed at tourists.
Goma is a tourist city in the Democratic Republic of Congo. The city is located near Rwanda, in the far east.
In 2002, Goma was destroyed as the Nyiragongo volcano spewed lava and most of the city's streets, and in particular the city centre, were buried.
Although Goma itself is relatively safe, you have to check for visits outside Goma the state of affairs regarding the battles that are going on in the province of North Kivu.
In addition, the city is the base for the ascension of the Nyiragongo Volcano and you’ll find some of the cheapest trips for Mountain Gorilla tracking in Africa.
With boda-boda (a motorcycle taxi) you can move on Goma. The normal (local) price is about 500 Congolese Francs for the short ride.
'Timbuktu' is relatively poorly accessible and is therefore used today as a metaphor for exotic, distant countries.
Today, Timbuktu is an impoverished city, although the reputation of the city makes it a tourist attraction and has an airport.
In 1990 it was added to the list of endangered world heritage sites because of desert storms.
It was one of the most important stopping spots of the PBS exhibition Special wonders from Henry Louis Gates' African world.
The city differs from the other cities in the country, because it has a more Arab appearance than an African one.
Kruger National Park (KNP) can be found in the northeast of South Africa and runs to the east along the border with Mozambique, in the north along the border with Zimbabwe and the southern border is the Krokodil River.
19,500 square kilometers is the park, divided into 14 different eco-zones, where various wild animal species are kept.
As an important attraction in South Africa, this park is the showpiece of the South African National Parks (SANParks).
Like all South African national parks, daily conservation allowances and entrance fees apply.
It can also be useful to buy a Wild Card. These offer either access to certain parts of parks in South Africa or to all national parks in South Africa.
The entire territory of Hong Kong is named after the island of Hong Kong and that is considered by many tourists as the most important place.
The large number of buildings that make up the Hong Kong skyline has already been compared to a shimmering rod chart that becomes visible thanks to Victoria Harbour's waters.
For the best views of Hong Kong you leave the island and head towards the waterfront of Kowloon across the street.
The vast majority of the population of the islange of Hong Kong lives very close to each other on won land along the northern coast.
This is where the British colonists established themselves, so if you're looking for evidence of the area's colonial past, then you're a good start here.
The Sundarbans are the largest mangrove forests in the whole world and extend 80 km (50 miles) from the coast to the Native American and Bengalian interior.
The Sundarbans are now officially included on the UNESCO World Heritage List. The section within the Indian borders is called the Sundarbans National Park.
The forests, however, are more than just mangrove swamps—they also feature some of the last mighty stretches of jungle that ever covered the Gangetic plain.
The Sundarbans cover an area of 3,850 km2, of which is a third peat and marsh area.
The Sundarbans have been a wildlife sanctuary since 1966, and in the area there are now an estimated 400 Bengalian tigers and about 30,000 axis deer.
During the day, buses depart from the station on the border of the districts (opposite the river). Most depart between 6.30 and 7.30pm, especially in the direction of the east and Jakar/Bumthang.
It is wise to buy a ticket a few days earlier, because the regional buses are often fully booked.
In most neighborhoods, small Japanese Coaster buses run which are comfortable and robust.
With shared taxis one can travel quickly and comfortably to nearby places, such as Paro (150 ngultrum) and Punakha (200 ngultrum).
The Oyapock bridge is a cable bridge crossing the Oyapock river to connect the Brazilian city of Oiapoque and the Franco-Guyanese city of Saint-Georges de l'Oyapock.
The two towers have a height of 83 meters. The building has a length of 378 meters and has two passageways with a width of 3.50 meters.
Under the bridge, the passage height is 15 meters. In August 2011, the construction of the bridge was completed, but it only opened for traffic in March 2017.
According to the planning, the bridge is fully operational in September 2017. Brazilian customs posts are expected to be ready for use.
The Guaraní was the most notable indigenous group. They lived in the area that is now Eastern Paraguay, lived as semi-nomadic hunters and also did self-sufficient agriculture.
In Chaco province lived other indigenous tribes, including the Guaycurú and Payaguá, who found their food by hunting, fishing and collecting.
Paraguay, formerly known as 'the great province of India', originated in the 16th century when Spanish settlers encountered the indigenous population.
A three-century colonization period followed among the Spanish.
Asunción was founded in 1537 and since then Paraguay has retained much of its indigenous character and identity.
Argentina is known for having one of the best polo teams and players in the world.
In December the biggest tournament of the year will take place on the polo fields in Las Cañitas.
Here you can also see smaller tournaments and competitions at other times in the year.
Check the Asociación Argentina de Polo for more information about tournaments and buying tickets for polo matches.
The official currency of the Falkland Islands is the Falkland Island pound (FKP). Its value is about one British pound (GBP).
On the islands there is only one bank, namely in Stanley opposite the shop FIC West. Here you can exchange money.
In general, British pounds are accepted all over the islands, and in Stanley you can also often pay with credit cards and U.S. dollars.
On the remote islands, you probably can’t pay with a credit card, but probably with the British and U.S. currencies. Ask the owners in advance which way you can pay.
Swap your money again before you leave the islands, because Falkland currency is very difficult to exchange outside.
Montevideo is below the equator, so when it's summer there it's winter in the northern hemisphere and vice versa.
Montevideo is located in the subtropics. In the summer months, temperatures higher than +30 ° C occur safely.
The winter can be deceptively cold: the temperature almost never goes below zero, but the wind in combination with the humidity makes it feel colder than the thermometer indicates.
The rain level remains approximately the same throughout the year, without recognizable 'wet' and 'dry' periods.
Many of the animals in the park are used to seeing people, but wild animals are ultimately wild. That is why they should not be fed or disturbed.
Keep in the park at least 100 meters away from bears and wolves, and 25 meters from all other wildlife.
Mooses, bison, reindeer, bears and just about all other large animals can attack you, no matter how tame they seem.
Every year, dozens of visitors are injured because they don’t keep an appropriate distance. These animals are large, wild and possibly dangerous, so give them space.
In addition, you should be aware that scents attract bears and other wildlife, so avoid wearing or cooking fragrant food and keep the camping spot clean.
The capital of Samoa is Apia and the city with almost 40,000 inhabitants is located on the island of Upolu.
Around the year 1850 Apia was founded and it is the official capital of Samoa from 1959.
In 1889, seven ships from Germany, the U.S. and Great Britain did not want to leave the port. This later became known as the infamous stalemate.
With the exception of a British battleship, all ships were sunk. Nearly 200 Americans and Germans lost their lives.
In the independence struggle by the Mau movement, the supreme leader, Tupua Tamasese Lealofi III, perished at an out of control non-violent gathering in the city.
There are many beaches, mainly because of the two ports of Auckland. The most popular are located in three areas.
The beaches of North Shore in the North Harbour district stretch from north to south along the Pacific Ocean, from Long Bay to Devonport.
These are almost all sandy beaches where you can swim safely, and most have pohutukawa trees that provide shade.
At Waitemata's port, in the luxury suburbs of Mission Bay and St Heliers, located in Central Auckland, you'll find the Tamaki Drive beaches.
These family beaches are sometimes crowded and have a good range of shops on the coast. Swimming is not unsafe.
'Number One' is the most important local beer that is not a complex beer, but pleasant and refreshing. The other local beer has the name 'Manta'.
There are a lot of French wines, but the New Zealand and Australian wines may be better suited for travel.
The local drinking water can simply be drunk safely, but bottled water is also easy to find if you don't trust it.
A 'flat white' is a strange concept for Australians. Black coffee is 'espresso', cappuccino has a lot of coffee milk (without foam) and tea is served without milk.
The hot chocolate is of Belgian quality. Fruit juices are expensive, but great.
There are trips to the reef throughout the year and injuries related to these trips to the reef are rare.
Nevertheless, ask for expert advice and follow all signs and safety warnings.
Cube jellyfish occur from October to April near beaches and estuaries north of Town of 1770. Sometimes they also occur outside this period.
Sharks do occur, but they rarely attack people. The majority of sharks are afraid of people and would just swim away.
The main habitat of saltwater crocodiles is located in the estuaries north of Rockhampton, and they don't normally live in the ocean.
Pre-reservation ensures peace of mind with the traveler, knowing that he has a place to sleep when he arrives at his destination.
Travel agencies often have deals with certain hotels, although you can usually book other accommodation types, such as a camping site, through a travel agency.
Travel agencies often offer packages with breakfast and transport to and from the airport and sometimes even packages with flight and hotel.
They can also hold your reservation if you want to think about the offer a little longer or if you need to acquire documents for your destination (e.g. visa).
However, if you have a request or want to make a change, you need to do so through the travel agency instead of the hotel.
For some festivals, the majority of attendees at musical festivals choose to camp on the spot and most visitors consider this to be an important part of the experience.
If you want to be close to the action, you need to be early to get hold of a camping spot near the music.
And remember the following: even when the music on the main stages is finished, music may be played on other parts of the festival site until the late hours.
For families whose children are still young, there are special campsites at some festivals.
Pay close attention to where your cabin is if you cross the Baltic Sea in winter, because the trip through the ice makes a huge noise. if you are too close.
Cruises to Saint Petersburg include time to explore the city. Cruise passengers are exempt from the visa requirements (check the conditions).
Casinos are usually committed to getting the most out of the time and money guests spend. Windows and clocks are not normally present and the exit is sometimes hard to find.
They normally have special offers on food, drinks and entertainment to keep them in a good mood and to avoid leaving.
Some locations offer free alcoholic beverages. However, when people are drunk, that affects their judgment and all seasoned gamblers know it’s hugely important to stay sober.
If you are going into the mountains or driving over mountain passes, you have to keep in mind that there may be snow or ice and the temperature can be very low.
On icy and snowy roads there is little friction and it drives differently than asphalt.
During snowstorms there may be enough snow in a very short period of time to get stuck.
The visibility can also be obstructed by falling or blowing snow or because there is condensation or ice on the windows of the vehicle.
On the other hand, ice and snow are normal in many countries and traffic is not hindered by this.
The biggest tourist African attraction are safaris, which for many visitors are the highlight of their trip.
The concept of safari refers in popular use to trips overland to see the beautiful African wildlife, particularly on the savannah.
Some animals, such as elephants and giraffes, often come close to cars, and a standard equipment allows good views.
If you want to see lions, cheetahs and leopards, you’ll need binoculars. Otherwise, there’s little chance you’ll see them.
A walking safari (also called a 'forest walk' or 'walking safari') means that you walk for several hours or days in a row.
The Paralympics are from August 24 to September 5, 2021. Some parts are played at other venues in Japan.
Tokyo becomes the only Asian city where the Olympics took place twice. The first time was in 1964.
If you have already booked flights and accommodation for 2020 before the postponement was announced, you can be in a difficult situation.
The cancellation policy varies, but from the end of March, most coronavirus-based cancellation policy lines are no longer valid until July 2020, when the Olympics were scheduled.
According to expectations, most tickets for events cost between ¥2,500 and ¥130,000. Normal tickets go around ¥7,000 fees.
You can dry damp clothes by ironing them. Many hotels have an iron and an ironing board available. You can borrow these things often, even if they are not in the room.
If there is no iron available or if you do not want to wear ironed socks, you can also use a hairdryer if available.
Make sure that the fabric does not get too hot (this can cause the fabric to shrink or, in extreme cases, scorching).
You can purify water in a variety of ways. Some ways are effective to counter specific risks.
In some areas it is enough to boil water for a minute, in other areas water should be boiled for several minutes.
Not every filter is equally effective. In case of doubt, it is best to drink water from a closed bottle from a reliable company.
