Europe is a relatively small continent, but with many independent countries. Normally, travelers between different countries have to apply for visas several times and undergo passport checks.
However, the Schengen area functions almost as one country in this area.
As long as you are staying in this zone, you can usually cross the border without having to undergo a passport check again.
When you have a Schengen visa, you do not have to apply for a visa for each Schengen country separately, which saves time, money and paperwork.
