Emergency weather is the general term for any dangerous weather phenomenon that can lead to damage, serious social disruption or the loss of human lives.
Extreme weather conditions can occur anywhere in the world. There are different types of weather conditions, which vary based on geography, topography and atmospheric conditions.
Phenomenons and consequences of severe weather are, for example, strong winds, hail, large amounts of precipitation and forest fires, but also thunderstorms, tornadoes, waters and hurricanes.
Snowstorms, ice storms and dust storms include examples of regional and seasonally extreme weather phenomena.
Travellers are strongly advised to be aware of the risks that severe weather conditions entail in their environment, as they can also influence some travel plans.
