Christmas is one of Christianity's most important holidays, celebrating the birth of Jesus.
Moreover, people who do not believe in Christian countries and non-Christians all over the world have adopted many traditions associated with the holiday.
There is a tradition in which you stay up the entire Easter night until at some point you can see the sunrise.
Obviously, there are Christian theological explanations for this tradition, but it might as well be a pre-Christian spring and fertility ritual.
In traditional churches, an Easter vigil is often held on the Saturday evening of the Easter weekend. The congregations often often celebrate a feast at midnight in honor of the resurrection of Christ.
